[agent:result] query: Databricks Vector Search API create index embedding_vector_column
[agent:result] answer: To create a Databricks Vector Search index with a precomputed embedding vector column, you use the `create_delta_sync_index` method from the `VectorSearchClient`. The embedding vector column must be of type `array[float]`. If you want to sync only the primary key and the embedding column, specify them in the `columns_to_sync` parameter.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] Here’s an example in Python:
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] ```python
[agent:result] from databricks.vector_search.client import VectorSearchClient
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] client = VectorSearchClient()
[agent:result] index = client.create_delta_sync_index(
[agent:result]     endpoint_name="your_vector_search_endpoint",
[agent:result]     source_table_name="your_catalog.your_schema.your_table",
[agent:result]     index_name="your_catalog.your_schema.your_index",
[agent:result]     primary_key="id",
[agent:result]     embedding_vector_column="text_vector",  # your precomputed embedding column
[agent:result]     columns_to_sync=["id", "text_vector"]  # sync only primary key and embedding column
[agent:result] )
[agent:result] ```
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] - The `embedding_vector_column` parameter is used when your source table already contains precomputed embeddings.
[agent:result] - The `columns_to_sync` parameter allows you to specify which columns to sync to the vector index. If not specified, all columns are synced, but the primary key and embedding vector column are always synced by default.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] For more details, see the [Databricks Vector Search documentation](https://docs.databricks.com/aws/en/vector-search/create-vector-search).
