[agent:result] answer: For a Databricks Vector Search DIRECT_ACCESS index, the embedding vector column must be of type array[float]. When creating the index via the REST API or Python SDK, you must specify the primary key and the embedding vector column. The embedding vector column is always synced to the index, along with the primary key. If you are using precomputed embeddings, ensure your source table contains a column of type array[float] for the embeddings. For storage-optimized endpoints, the embedding dimension must be evenly divisible by 16.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] Here’s a summary of the key points:
[agent:result] - The embedding vector column must be of type array[float].
[agent:result] - The column is always synced to the index, along with the primary key.
[agent:result] - For storage-optimized endpoints, the embedding dimension must be divisible by 16.
[agent:result] - You must use the REST API or Python SDK to create and manage DIRECT_ACCESS indexes; the UI is not supported.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] For more details, see the [Databricks documentation on creating vector search indexes](https://docs.databricks.com/aws/en/vector-search/create-vector-search).
