[agent:result] query: Databricks vector search index direct access schema_json embedding_vector_column Terraform
[agent:result] answer: For a Databricks Vector Search Index of type DIRECT_ACCESS in Terraform, you need to specify the `schema_json` and `embedding_vector_column` parameters. Here’s how you can define it:
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] - **schema_json**: This is a required JSON string that defines the schema of your index, including the embedding vector column and any metadata columns. The embedding vector column must be of type `array<float>`.
[agent:result] - **embedding_vector_column**: This is the name of the column in your schema that contains the embedding vectors. It is required if you are not using `embedding_source_columns` (which is for Delta Sync indexes).
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] Here’s an example Terraform resource block for a DIRECT_ACCESS index:
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] ```hcl
[agent:result] resource "databricks_vector_search_index" "direct_access_index" {
[agent:result]   name           = "catalog.schema.index_name"
[agent:result]   endpoint_name  = databricks_vector_search_endpoint.this.name
[agent:result]   index_type     = "DIRECT_ACCESS"
[agent:result]   primary_key    = "id"
[agent:result]   embedding_dimension = 3072 # Replace with your embedding dimension
[agent:result]   embedding_vector_column = "text_vector" # Name of the column containing embedding vectors
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]   schema_json = jsonencode({
[agent:result]     id           = "string"
[agent:result]     text         = "string"
[agent:result]     text_vector  = "array<float>"
[agent:result]     source       = "string" # Optional metadata column
[agent:result]   })
[agent:result] }
[agent:result] ```
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] **Key Points:**
[agent:result] - `schema_json` must include all columns, with the embedding vector column specified as `array<float>`.
[agent:result] - `embedding_vector_column` must match the name of the embedding vector column in your schema.
[agent:result] - `primary_key` is required and must be a column in your schema.
[agent:result] - `embedding_dimension` is required for DIRECT_ACCESS indexes and must match the dimension of your embeddings.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] For more details, see the [Terraform registry documentation](https://registry.terraform.io/providers/databricks/databricks/1.65.1/docs/resources/vector_search_index) and the [Databricks Vector Search API docs](https://docs.databricks.com/aws/en/vector-search/create-vector-search).
