[agent:result] query: "Exactly one valid embedding_vector_column must be specified" Databricks
[agent:result] answer: The error message "Exactly one valid embedding_vector_column must be specified" in Databricks typically occurs when you are creating or using a vector search index and you have not correctly specified the embedding vector column. This column must be of type array[float] and must be explicitly provided when creating a Delta Sync Index or when performing a vector search.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] Here are the key points to resolve this issue:
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] - When creating a Delta Sync Index, you must specify exactly one embedding_vector_column if you are using precomputed embeddings. This column should contain your embedding vectors and must be of type array[float].
[agent:result] - If you are using a model endpoint to generate embeddings, you should specify embedding_source_column and embedding_model_endpoint_name instead of embedding_vector_column.
[agent:result] - Ensure that you are not specifying multiple embedding_vector_column values or leaving it unspecified when it is required.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] For example, in the Python SDK, your call might look like this:
[agent:result] ```python
[agent:result] create_delta_sync_index_and_wait(
[agent:result]     endpoint_name="your_endpoint",
[agent:result]     index_name="your_index",
[agent:result]     primary_key="id",
[agent:result]     source_table_name="your_table",
[agent:result]     pipeline_type="DIRECT_ACCESS",
[agent:result]     embedding_vector_column="your_embedding_column"  # Must be specified and valid
[agent:result] )
[agent:result] ```
[agent:result] If you are still encountering the error, double-check that:
[agent:result] - The column name is correct and exists in your table.
[agent:result] - The column is of type array[float].
[agent:result] - You are not specifying both embedding_vector_column and embedding_source_column/embedding_model_endpoint_name at the same time, unless required by your use case.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] If you need more specific guidance, please share the code or command you are using to create or query the index.
